<title>UK: British output prices rise 0.5 pct in December.</title>
<headline>British output prices rise 0.5 pct in December.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>British output prices, a key indicator of inflation, rose 0.5 percent in December for a 1.7 percent year-on-year increase, official data showed on Monday.</p>
<p>Input prices fell 0.5 percent seasonally adjusted for a 5.9 percent year-on-year fall. The data were in line with analysts' expectations.</p>
